              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Dry van trailers are the backbone of the freight industry. From consumer goods and retail shipments to industrial supplies, they move a significant portion of the country's cargo every day. If you're expanding your fleet or starting a trucking operation, you may be wondering about the standard size of a dry van trailer and which option makes the most sense for your routes and freight.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-standard-size",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Standard Size of a Dry Van Trailer",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "standard-size"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-standard-size-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When people talk about the standard size of a dry van trailer, they're usually referring to the 53 ft dry van trailer. This size has become the industry standard for long-haul freight because it offers the best balance between cargo capacity and road regulations.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-standard-size-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>A typical 53 ft dry van trailer offers:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-standard-size-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "53 feet"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "About 100–102 inches"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Roughly 110 inches"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Up to 45,000 pounds, depending on configuration"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Generally around 26 standard pallets"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-standard-size-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The extra length compared to smaller trailers allows carriers to move more freight per trip, which can significantly improve revenue and reduce cost per mile. For many owner-operators, investing in a 53 ft dry van trailer for sale is one of the most practical decisions when building or expanding a freight operation.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-standard-size-5-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-standard-size-5",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
